title: The Strike Committee Says No
subtitle: A district strike committee defies the Zentrale
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year >= 1919 and year <= 1920 and time >= 6 and crisis = 0 and congress = 0 and ending_id = 0 and strike_count >= 1 and e20_committee_line = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 1
on-arrival: {!
var d = RG.target('strike');
Q.e20_committee_d = d;
Q.e20_committee_name = Q.sys_target_name;
Q.e20_committee_trade = Q.sys_target_trade;
Q.e20_committee_ours = Q.sys_target_ours;
Q.e20_committee_faction = Q.sys_target_faction_name;
Q.e20_committee_nb = Q.sys_target_neighbour_name ? 1 : 0;
Q.e20_committee_nb_name = Q.sys_target_neighbour_name || 0;
Q.e20_committee_rep = Q.sys_target_repression;
!}

= The Strike Committee Says No

In [+ e20_committee_name +], [+ e20_committee_trade +] have been out for weeks. The strike committee is elected in the works, and our comrades sit on it, [? if e20_committee_ours = 1 : most of them loyal to the Zentrale ?][? if e20_committee_ours = 0 : most of them followers of the [+ e20_committee_faction +], not of the Zentrale ?]. The Zentrale has told them that the strike cannot win alone and must be ended in good order before the police end it for them.

The committee has voted the Zentrale's letter down, and printed the vote. It wants the party to call out the neighbouring districts instead. [? if e20_committee_rep >= 55 : The Security Police are already in the town in force. ?]

- @back: Back the committee: the strikers know their own fight.
- @spread: Call on the neighbouring districts to come out in solidarity.
- @order: Order our comrades off the committee, and the strike ended.
- @envoy: Send a member of the Zentrale to lead the strike.

@back
subtitle: The district's loyalty grows, and the Zentrale's authority shrinks. The strike goes on.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e20_committee_line = 1;
RG.district(Q.e20_committee_d, {loyalty: 8, militancy: 4, repression: 4});
Q.unity -= 3;
Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 3;
Q.offensive_satisfaction += 4;
Q.lean_offensive += 1;
!}

The Zentrale publishes a short note: the comrades in [+ e20_committee_name +] are the best judges of their own struggle. The committee reads it out at the gates, to cheers. In other districts, secretaries wonder what else they may decide for themselves.

@spread
subtitle: [? if lock_councils = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The Left's answer. A bigger strike, or a bigger defeat.
view-if: e20_committee_nb = 1
choose-if: lock_councils < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids it.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_councils == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.e20_committee_line = 2;
RG.spreadStrike(Q.e20_committee_d);
RG.district(Q.e20_committee_d, {loyalty: 6, repression: 6});
Q.repression += 2;
Q.offensive_satisfaction += 6;
Q.unionist_satisfaction -= 4;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
RG.ecci('bukharin', 3);
!}

Our couriers carry the committee's appeal to [+ e20_committee_nb_name +]. By the end of the week the works there are out too, and the police have twice as many pickets to break.

@order
subtitle: The Spartacist discipline. The strike ends, the district is bitter, and the party keeps its word to itself.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e20_committee_line = 3;
RG.endStrike(Q.e20_committee_d);
RG.district(Q.e20_committee_d, {loyalty: -14, members: -0.04});
Q.unity += 2;
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction += 4;
Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 4;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
!}

Our comrades resign from the committee, and the strike crumbles within days. In [+ e20_committee_name +], the workers who went back say the communists left them alone at the gate. Some tear up their cards.

@envoy
subtitle: Costs 1 fund. The Right's way: take the strike in hand, win what can be won, and end it with a settlement.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no funds to send anyone.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e20_committee_line = 4;
Q.resources -= 1;
if (Math.random() < 0.55) {
    RG.endStrike(Q.e20_committee_d, 'won');
    Q.e20_committee_ok = 1;
} else {
    RG.endStrike(Q.e20_committee_d);
    Q.e20_committee_ok = 0;
}
RG.district(Q.e20_committee_d, {loyalty: 3});
Q.worker_support += 2;
Q.unionist_satisfaction += 5;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
!}

[? if e20_committee_ok = 1 : The Zentrale's man sits down with the employers and the union officials, and comes out with a wage rise and no victimisations. The committee grumbles, and takes it. ?][? if e20_committee_ok = 0 : The Zentrale's man negotiates for three days and comes out with a promise of arbitration. The strike ends without a victory, but without a rout. ?]
